  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#default-fetch-and-process-the-linked-resource\r\n\r\nThis doesn't say anything about the element being [browsing-context connected](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#browsing-context-connected), like `<link rel=stylesheet>` and `<link rel=modulepreload>` do, suggesting that fetches can happen even when the element is not in the DOM. It seems to me it should check for that for most if not all `rel` values.\r\n\r\nDemo for `rel=preload`: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/9210",
